      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأَمَّمَ</span></b>  and 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَيَمَّمَ</span></b> : see 1, former part, in four
places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تأمّم بِهِ</span>: see 8. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَّمْتُ</span> <i>I took for
myself,</i> or <i>adopted, a mother.</i> (S.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأَمَّمَهَا</span>
<i>He took her for himself,</i> or <i>adopted her, as a
mother;</i> (S, * M, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استآمّها</span></b> , (M, K,)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأَمَّهَهَا</span>. (M.)

